# Line-ending policy — ticket 02 (steam-release map), ruled by Henry 2026-08-21.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Before it, the repo had no policy and the blobs proved it:
# 339 tracked files stored CRLF, 340 stored LF, 11 stored mixed. The desktop sync
# layer periodically rewrote the working tree to CRLF, which made ~160 files show
# as modified with insertions == deletions and zero content change (the sweep that
# `_WARNING-line-endings.md` documented). With no consistent baseline in the index
# there was nothing to restore *to*, so the sweep kept coming back.
#
# THE RULE. `text=auto` normalizes every text file to LF **in the repository**;
# `eol=crlf` checks it back out as CRLF **in the working tree**, which is what the
# Windows-side sync layer wants anyway. Because the clean filter strips CR on the
# way in, a working-tree file is byte-identical to its blob whether it holds LF or
# CRLF — so an ending flip can no longer register as a diff, in either direction.
#
# Landed together with `git add --renormalize -u`, which rewrote every blob to LF
# in one commit. Do not revert one without the other.

* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binary — never touched by the clean/smudge filters, and never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.wav  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.tgz  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they break under bash/CI even on Windows checkouts.
*.sh   text eol=lf
